        <p class="profile-detail-region">Battle · Europe</p>
        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Battle of Mohács</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Date</span><span class="info-stat-val">29 August 1526, in the afternoon</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Place</span><span class="info-stat-val">A wide, waterlogged plain near the village of Mohács in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-hungary">Kingdom of Hungary</a>, on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a></span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">The two sides</span><span class="info-stat-val">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-hungary">Kingdom of Hungary</a> under King Louis II, with some 25,000 to 30,000 men at Mohács; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suleiman-the-magnificent">Suleiman the Magnificent</a> and the grand <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vizier">vizier</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pargali-ibrahim-pasha">Pargalı Ibrahim Pasha</a>, perhaps 50,000, though some contemporary and modern historians put the number at 100,000</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Outcome</span><span class="info-stat-val">The Hungarian army was encircled and its lines collapsed within two hours; King Louis II drowned in flight. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buda">Buda</a>, then withdrew.</span></div>
        </div>
