    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Estimates of the Ottoman army run from about 45,000 to 100,000, while the Hungarians numbered some 25,000 to 30,000; the figures differ from passage to passage and between historians.</li><li>The Hungarian charge drove back the Ottoman front line, but Ibrahim Pasha's centre fell back in a crescent and the Hungarians, caught in the open between wings, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cannon">cannon</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/janissaries">Janissary</a> fire, were encircled.</li><li>King Louis II and more than 1,000 nobles died, and about 2,000 captured Hungarians were executed afterwards; the kingdom was later split in three, and Hungarians still say 'More was lost at Mohács'.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>King Louis II drowned in the marshy ground by the Csele stream, weighed down by his armour, and his body was found weeks later buried in the mud.</p></aside>
    </section>

